  "id": "DrugBank_DB05578 - MONDO_8903",
  "verbalization": "Ramucirumab is implicated in the pathogenesis of Lung Cancer through its association with Non-small Cell Lung Carcinoma (NSCLC), as evidenced by its indications for this disease. The drug is linked to NSCLC via intermediate agents—Gefitinib, Crizotinib, and Olmutinib—each of which is also indicated for NSCLC. This suggests a potential pathway where Ramucirumab may influence NSCLC through a shared mechanism of action, possibly involving tumor cell proliferation or survival pathways. The consistent clinical indication across these agents supports a mechanistic link between Ramucirumab and NSCLC, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated. The evidence is robust, but further investigation is needed to confirm the direct relationship and to understand the specific biological processes involved.",
